@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix gufo: <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix fno: <https://w3id.org/function/ontology#> .

gmeow:Scenario
    a logic:Kind ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Scenario"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Entity ;
    skos:definition "A hypothesized situation under consideration — a context that entertains a supposition without asserting it. One of the distinct typed contexts of the logic context algebra, kept apart from a logic:PossibleWorld (an alethic possibility), a gmeow:Standpoint (a named perspective), and a gmeow:State (one state of affairs along a logic:Path): entertaining a scenario is neither claiming it is possible nor adopting a perspective on it. The logic: accessibility machinery stays central in the logic slice and is referenced here in prose only, with no asserted logic: triples."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:fundingShortfall a gmeow:Scenario ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid conflating it with a logic:PossibleWorld (entertaining a scenario does not assert its alethic possibility) or with a gmeow:Standpoint (a scenario is a hypothesized situation, not a perspective truth is held relative to)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Mint a Scenario to entertain a supposition as a context under consideration; hold its contents according to it without asserting them in the base graph, and reason within it under context-indexed entailment, with no implicit union with other contexts."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name a hypothesized situation under consideration as a first-class context — when a supposition is entertained and reasoned within without being asserted as actual or as alethically possible."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:Standpoint
    a logic:Kind ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "Coexistence is explicitly permitted: contradictory gmeow:accordingTo-scoped claims over the same subject/predicate are co-equal and must NOT be flagged — there is deliberately no constraint on their coexistence (Principle 9, no single slot to win). This is the intent the retired documentation-only gmeow:StandpointCoexistenceShape recorded: coexistence is proven by the positive fixtures, not by a SHACL constraint, because the OWL-infers / SHACL-validates split means SHACL only ever rejects closed-world malformations, never co-equal contradiction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Standpoint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:instantiatesFramework logic:ModalFramework ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Entity ;
    skos:definition "A named perspective / frame within which claims are held true — a state's official position, a community's usage, an editorial or historiographic point of view. Minted only when the frame needs its own identity and labels; often a bare gmeow:Agent (a polity, an organization) suffices as the value of gmeow:accordingTo instead. Standpoints form a poset under gmeow:sharpens, topped by gmeow:universalStandpoint."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:ottomanView a gmeow:Standpoint ; gmeow:sharpens gmeow:universalStandpoint ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid minting one when a bare gmeow:Agent (a polity, an organization) already suffices as the gmeow:accordingTo value, and never treat one standpoint as the primary or preferred frame — competing standpoints coexist as co-equal vantages, none privileged (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Mint the Standpoint, order it under gmeow:sharpens (every standpoint except gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint sharpens gmeow:universalStandpoint — silence sits outside the refinement order), and reference it from a statement via gmeow:accordingTo or from a reified gmeow:Observation via gmeow:vantage; an unindexed statement is held in gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint by default — unspecified, not universal; only an explicit gmeow:universalStandpoint index propagates as universal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to mint a named frame as a first-class vantage — when a state's official position, a community's usage, or an editorial point of view needs its own identity, labels, or place in the gmeow:sharpens poset to be the value of gmeow:accordingTo or gmeow:vantage."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:StandpointModality
    a logic:AbstractIndividualType ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Standpoint Modality"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:instantiatesFramework logic:ModalFramework ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    skos:definition "The belief value a standpoint assigns a proposition — a closed value vocabulary spanning the Standpoint-Logic □/◊ and the CRMinf belief value (true/false/probable/possible), plus the Frankfurt bullshit modality: gmeow:unequivocal, gmeow:probable, gmeow:conceivable, gmeow:refuted, gmeow:bullshit. Absence of a value is read as unequivocal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:standpointModality gmeow:refuted ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid conflating it with gmeow:confidence (our certainty about the stance) or with gmeow:accordingTo (whose frame); modality is how settled the standpoint itself holds the claim, an axis orthogonal to those. Never use a refuted value to mark a proposition globally false — refutation is one standpoint's denial, never a winner over the rest (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Reference the seeded modality individuals from a StandpointClaim via gmeow:claimModality or from an annotated statement via gmeow:standpointModality; leave the value absent to mean unequivocal, and keep competing modalities on coexisting claims rather than resolving them."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the value vocabulary for HOW a standpoint holds a proposition — the closed set of belief values (unequivocal, probable, conceivable, refuted, bullshit) a claim declares through gmeow:standpointModality or gmeow:claimModality."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:StandpointTenure
    a logic:Situation ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Standpoint Tenure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:TimeScopedRelation ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty gmeow:tenureStandpoint ;
            owl:someValuesFrom gmeow:Standpoint ;
        ] ,
        [
            a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty gmeow:standpointClaim ;
            owl:someValuesFrom gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
        ] ;
    skos:definition "The reified, time-scoped fact that a standpoint held a particular position over an interval — recognition granted in 2008 and withdrawn in 2030 is an opened-then-closed tenure, never a deletion (Principle 10). Use only when the adoption / withdrawal of the position is itself worth modelling; the common case is a bare gmeow:accordingTo annotation. Carries its standpoint-time interval via gmeow:duringInterval (temporal module). A StandpointTenure generates a gmeow:standpointClaim observation. The tenure is the time-scoped fact; the claim is the observation of that fact. The tenureStandpoint maps to the claim's vantage; the tenurePosition maps to the claim's observedFeature."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:recognition a gmeow:StandpointTenure ; gmeow:tenureStandpoint ex:stateA ; gmeow:duringInterval ex:2008to2030 ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid reifying a tenure for an ordinary perspectival claim — the common case is a bare gmeow:accordingTo annotation, reify on demand (Principle 4) — and avoid deleting a withdrawn position; close the tenure with gmeow:displayable false instead, and never elevate one tenure as the authoritative position."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernDisclosure ,
        gmeow:concernStandpoints ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Mint the tenure, bind its frame with gmeow:tenureStandpoint and the held claim with gmeow:tenurePosition, scope it in standpoint-time via gmeow:duringInterval (temporal module); it generates exactly one gmeow:standpointClaim observation whose vantage is the tenureStandpoint and whose observedFeature is the tenurePosition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the adoption or withdrawal of a standpoint's position over an interval is itself the fact of interest — recognition granted then revoked — so the change is an opened-then-closed tenure carrying its standpoint-time interval, retained never deleted (Principle 10)."@x-gmeow-english .

# A gmeow:tenurePosition value IS, by definition, a reified statement — the standpoint-indexed
# claim the tenure held (it surfaces as the gmeow:observedFeature of the generated
# gmeow:StandpointClaim, and StandpointClaim is an gmeow:Observation). So a gmeow:StandpointTenure
# that records its held position as a bare, unreified triple is ill-formed. This obligation is
# authored in the classic RDF reification form the validation-shape derivation reads (rdf:Statement +
# rdf:subject/rdf:predicate/rdf:object): a reifier typed with the shape the reifier must conform to
# (gmeow:Observation), reifying the schema-level gmeow:tenurePosition triple. It lowers to a
# property shape on gmeow:tenurePosition carrying sh:reifierShape gmeow:Observation-shape +
# sh:reificationRequired true — the one closed-world obligation with no ordinary-OWL antecedent, so
# it rides the statement layer rather than a shape vocabulary. The classic form (not the native
# rdf:reifies <<( )>> term) is used because a quoted-triple object cannot ride the base-quad fold to
# gmeow.gts. The reifier IS an observation (Principle 9: a statement promoted to a reified
# gmeow:Observation), which is why typing it gmeow:Observation is faithful, not a stub.
gmeow:tenurePositionReificationObligation
    a rdf:Statement ,
        gmeow:Observation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "tenure-position reification obligation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The authoring vehicle for the closed-world requirement that every gmeow:StandpointTenure records its gmeow:tenurePosition as a reified statement whose reifier conforms to gmeow:Observation-shape. Authored in the classic RDF reification form the validation-shape derivation reads, it is itself a well-formed reified observation — held from the universal standpoint, observing the standpoint claim — so it satisfies the observation shape it also declares."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ;
    gmeow:vantage gmeow:universalStandpoint ;
    gmeow:observedFeature gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    rdf:subject gmeow:StandpointTenure ;
    rdf:predicate gmeow:tenurePosition ;
    rdf:object gmeow:StandpointClaim .

gmeow:State
    a logic:Kind ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "State"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Entity ;
    skos:definition "One state of affairs along a history — the position (index) within a logic:Path that a logic:Situation realizes. DISTINCT from logic:Situation: the Situation is the reified state-of-affairs snapshot (the static counterpart of an Event), while a State is the position on the path at which a Situation is realized; succession between States along a path is the typed accessibility relation logic:temporallySucceeds. One of the distinct typed contexts of the logic context algebra; the relationship to logic:Situation and logic:Path is stated in prose, not as a subclass edge into a reasoned class."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:beforeMerge a gmeow:State ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using it for the reified state-of-affairs content — that is logic:Situation; a gmeow:State is the path position the Situation realizes. Avoid asserting State succession with the bare logic:accessibleFrom rather than the typed logic:temporallySucceeds."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Mint a State as a position along a logic:Path, realized by a logic:Situation; order States with logic:temporallySucceeds (a strict order) and read truth along the path under context-indexed entailment."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name one state of affairs along a history — a position on a logic:Path that a logic:Situation realizes — when path-relative truth or temporal succession of configurations must be modelled."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:accordingTo
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "according to"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint / frame within which the annotated statement is asserted true — *according to whom*. DISTINCT from gmeow:wasAttributedTo (which source RECORDED the claim) and gmeow:confidence (how sure we are); a claim may carry all three with no inferential bridge among them. Its value is a gmeow:Agent (a polity, community, or organization IRI) or a gmeow:Standpoint individual (a frame that needs its own identity). When a statement is promoted to a reified gmeow:Observation, gmeow:accordingTo becomes the gmeow:vantage of the relator (vantage ⊑ accordingTo — documented, not axiomatised, because accordingTo is an AnnotationProperty and vantage is an ObjectProperty). Standpoint-TIME — when the frame held this position — rides gmeow:validFrom / gmeow:validUntil on the same statement in the light case, or a reified gmeow:StandpointTenure when the adoption / withdrawal is itself the fact of interest. The range is intentionally open. An unindexed statement is held in gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint — unspecified, not universal; only an explicit gmeow:universalStandpoint index (or explicit quantification over all contexts of a stated type) propagates as universal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ,
        gmeow:concernStatementMetadata ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:bullshit
    a gmeow:StandpointModality ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "bullshit (indifference to truth)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint asserts P with indifference to its truth-value — Frankfurt's bullshit modality. Distinct from lying (which cares about truth and asserts the opposite) and from error (which cares and gets it wrong). A bullshit claim is neither true nor false under the standpoint; it is held without regard for correspondence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:decomposesToAxis gmeow:polarityAffirm ,
        gmeow:modalForceActual ,
        gmeow:credenceUnspecified ,
        gmeow:assertoricAssert ,
        gmeow:truthIndifferent ,
        gmeow:supportNeither ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:claimModality
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "claim modality"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:StandpointModality ;
    skos:definition "The modality (unequivocal, probable, conceivable, refuted, bullshit) assigned to a StandpointClaim. Semantically equivalent to observationResult for StandpointClaims, but not declared rdfs:subPropertyOf because StandpointModality (a gufo:QualityValue / abstract individual) is disjoint from gmeow:Entity (a gufo:Endurant) in the DL profile. When a StandpointClaim is flattened to an annotated statement, claimModality becomes standpointModality. PROJECTION SURFACE: the five-value modality is now the lossless projection of the six canonical axes (gmeow:claimPolarity, gmeow:claimModalForce, gmeow:claimCredence / gmeow:claimCredenceLevel, gmeow:claimAssertoricForce, gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness, gmeow:claimSupportStatus); author the axes, not this convenience twin."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:recognitionClaim gmeow:claimModality gmeow:unequivocal ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid for the produced value of a non-standpoint observation (use gmeow:observationResult) and avoid asserting two modalities — it is functional; a refuted value denies the claim from this frame, never marks it globally false (Principle 9). For new claims prefer the six canonical axes — this five-value twin is a generated projection surface, not a co-equal authoring path."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point the StandpointClaim at one gmeow:StandpointModality individual; when the claim is flattened to an annotated statement, this becomes gmeow:standpointModality, and an absent value reads as unequivocal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to assign the belief value a gmeow:StandpointClaim carries — the reified-relator counterpart of gmeow:standpointModality, used when a claim is a first-class observation rather than an annotated statement."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:conceivable
    a gmeow:StandpointModality ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "conceivable (◊, possible)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "◊_S — possible according to the standpoint: the proposition holds in some precisification the standpoint admits, but is not settled (CRMinf belief value 'possible')."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:decomposesToAxis gmeow:polaritySuspend ,
        gmeow:modalForcePossible ,
        gmeow:credencePossible ,
        gmeow:assertoricAssume ,
        gmeow:truthAimed ,
        gmeow:supportNeither ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:probable
    a gmeow:StandpointModality ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "probable"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Likely true according to the standpoint — held more strongly than merely possible, but short of settled (CRMinf belief value 'probable')."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:decomposesToAxis gmeow:polarityAffirm ,
        gmeow:modalForceActual ,
        gmeow:credenceLikely ,
        gmeow:assertoricConjecture ,
        gmeow:truthAimed ,
        gmeow:supportSupported ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:refuted
    a gmeow:StandpointModality ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "refuted (□¬, false)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "□¬_S — settled false according to the standpoint: the standpoint DENIES the proposition (CRMinf belief value 'false'). Distinct from silence (no claim) and from low gmeow:confidence — an explicit, recorded denial. The proposition is carried as the subject of the denial, never asserted as a fact of the universal standpoint."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:decomposesToAxis gmeow:polarityDeny ,
        gmeow:modalForceNecessary ,
        gmeow:credenceCertain ,
        gmeow:assertoricAssert ,
        gmeow:truthAimed ,
        gmeow:supportOpposed ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:sharpens
    a owl:ObjectProperty ,
        owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:Standpoint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "sharpens"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Standpoint ;
    skos:definition "S1 sharpens S2: every precisification S1 admits is also admitted by S2, so S1 is the more specific frame (the standpoint ⊆ / refinement relation of Standpoint Logic; CKR's coverage relation). Transitive. Every standpoint except gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint sharpens gmeow:universalStandpoint — the default-of-silence sits outside the refinement order and carries no gmeow:sharpens edge."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:cityCouncilView gmeow:sharpens ex:regionalView ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid reading it as a ranking that picks a winner — sharpening is containment, not preference, and the broader frame is not 'more true' than the sharper one; competing, incomparable standpoints simply both sharpen the universal standpoint (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Assert gmeow:sharpens from the more specific standpoint to the broader one and let transitivity build the poset; anchor every standpoint except gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint to gmeow:universalStandpoint at the top, and let a Standpoint-Logic reasoner read □/◊ entailments across the refinement order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to order two standpoints by precisification — when one frame is a strict refinement of another (every precisification it admits is admitted by the broader frame), building the standpoint poset whose top is gmeow:universalStandpoint."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:standpointClaim
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointTenure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "standpoint claim"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    skos:definition "The StandpointClaim observation that a StandpointTenure generates — the reified observation of the tenure's time-scoped fact. The tenure is the time-scoped situation; the claim is the observation of that fact. Functional: a tenure generates exactly one claim."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:recognition gmeow:standpointClaim ex:recognitionClaim ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid asserting more than one claim per tenure — it is functional, exactly one observation per tenure — and avoid hanging a free-standing StandpointClaim here when no tenure exists; mint the claim as a bare gmeow:Observation instead."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Generate one gmeow:StandpointClaim from the tenure, mapping gmeow:tenureStandpoint to the claim's gmeow:vantage and gmeow:tenurePosition to its gmeow:observedFeature; carry the modality on the claim via gmeow:claimModality."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to link a gmeow:StandpointTenure to the single gmeow:StandpointClaim observation it generates — the bridge from the time-scoped situation to its observation, so the tenure's position is queryable on the universal observation spine."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:standpointModality
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "standpoint modality"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:StandpointModality ;
    skos:definition "The belief value a standpoint assigns the annotated proposition — *how* the standpoint holds it, not merely *that* it holds it. This single axis is at least as expressive as BOTH the Standpoint-Logic modal operators (□_S / ◊_S) AND the CRMinf belief value (true / false / probable / possible): gmeow:unequivocal (□, settled true), gmeow:probable (likely true), gmeow:conceivable (◊, possible), gmeow:refuted (□¬, settled false — the standpoint DENIES the proposition), gmeow:bullshit (indifference to truth — Frankfurt). Optional; ABSENT is read as unequivocal. Orthogonal to gmeow:confidence (our certainty about the standpoint's stance) and gmeow:accordingTo (whose frame). Refutation is what lets GMEOW distinguish a standpoint's explicit denial from its silence — the neutral-stance ambiguity flat models cannot resolve. PROJECTION SURFACE: this five-value axis is now the lossless projection of the six canonical axes (gmeow:standpointPolarity, gmeow:standpointModalForce, gmeow:standpointCredence / gmeow:standpointCredenceLevel, gmeow:standpointAssertoricForce, gmeow:standpointTruthDirectedness, gmeow:standpointSupportStatus); author the axes, not this convenience twin."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ,
        gmeow:concernStatementMetadata ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:tenurePosition
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointTenure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "tenure position"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint-indexed claim the tenure says the standpoint held over its interval — a reified statement (a gmeow:StatementMetadata cell in the statement DSL). The range is intentionally left open: the statement-DSL spec layer is not part of the reasoned import closure, so asserting it as rdfs:range would dangle in the merged graph. When a StandpointTenure generates a StandpointClaim observation, the tenurePosition becomes the observedFeature of the claim."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:recognition gmeow:tenurePosition ex:statehoodClaim ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid for the holding frame (that is gmeow:tenureStandpoint) and avoid asserting the position as a fact of the universal standpoint — it is the proposition the frame held, one coexisting claim among competing tenures, never the resolved truth (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point the tenure at the reified statement it held (a statement-DSL cell); the range is left open because that spec layer is outside the reasoned import closure. It surfaces as the gmeow:observedFeature of the generated gmeow:standpointClaim."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name the standpoint-indexed claim a gmeow:StandpointTenure says the frame held over its interval — the reified statement that becomes the gmeow:observedFeature of the generated StandpointClaim."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:tenureStandpoint
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointTenure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "tenure standpoint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Standpoint ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint whose position a standpoint-tenure records. When a StandpointTenure generates a StandpointClaim observation, the tenureStandpoint becomes the vantage of the claim."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:recognition gmeow:tenureStandpoint ex:stateA ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid for the position held (that is gmeow:tenurePosition) and avoid assigning two standpoints to one tenure — it is functional, exactly one frame per tenure; a different frame's position is a separate tenure, never a privileged primary one (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point the tenure at one gmeow:Standpoint; it surfaces as the gmeow:vantage of the generated gmeow:standpointClaim, so generic consumers read 'whose frame' uniformly across tenures and bare observations."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to name the single standpoint whose position a gmeow:StandpointTenure records — the frame that becomes the gmeow:vantage of the generated StandpointClaim."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:unequivocal
    a gmeow:StandpointModality ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "unequivocal (□, true)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "□_S — settled / necessary true according to the standpoint: the proposition holds in every precisification the standpoint admits (CRMinf belief value 'true'). The default when no gmeow:standpointModality is given."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:decomposesToAxis gmeow:polarityAffirm ,
        gmeow:modalForceNecessary ,
        gmeow:credenceCertain ,
        gmeow:assertoricAssert ,
        gmeow:truthAimed ,
        gmeow:supportSupported ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:universalStandpoint
    a gmeow:Standpoint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "universal standpoint (*)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The universal standpoint * — the top of the poset, admitting every precisification: the uncontested global facts every standpoint shares. A statement with no gmeow:accordingTo is held in gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint, not the universal standpoint; universalStandpoint remains the explicit-universal top of the poset that every standpoint except gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint gmeow:sharpens."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint
    a gmeow:Standpoint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "unspecified standpoint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The default-of-silence standpoint: a statement asserted with no context index is held in gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint — unspecified, not universal. It is not implicitly true in every context, not in any particular context, and not at the top of the gmeow:sharpens poset; silence licenses no propagation. Only an explicit universal assertion — a statement indexed to gmeow:universalStandpoint, or one that explicitly quantifies over all contexts of a stated type — propagates as universal. Treating an unindexed statement as universally true is the world-semantics analogue of the closed-world collapse, manufacturing a claim the author never made. Contrast gmeow:universalStandpoint, which remains the explicit-universal top of the poset; gmeow:unspecifiedStandpoint sits outside the refinement order and carries no gmeow:sharpens edge in either direction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:gmeowBestPractice
    a gmeow:Standpoint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW best-practice standpoint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The named advisory vantage from which GMEOW's own best-practice recommendations (gmeow:deonticRecommendation) are issued — the root of the advisory standpoint sub-poset that per-domain style-guide standpoints gmeow:sharpens. Advice is one coequal standpoint's perspectival claim, never a global verdict: a gmeow:ComplianceAssessment issued from this vantage may coexist with a contrary assessment from another (Principle 9). It is the in-graph reconciliation of the advisory tier's issuing-standpoint IRI (the validate crate's BEST_PRACTICE_STANDPOINT_IRI)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:sharpens gmeow:universalStandpoint ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Factored claim modality.
# The closed 5-value gmeow:StandpointModality fuses four separable epistemic
# notions onto one axis. The six orthogonal canonical axes below are what claims
# author directly; the legacy five values are RETAINED as a lossless projection
# (see gmeow:decomposesToAxis bundles and crates/slice/src/standpoint_modality.rs).
# DL-clean: every axis class is rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue (disjoint from
# gmeow:Entity); the logic: machinery (Standpoint-Logic □/◊, Belnap support) stays
# central in slices/grounding/logic and is referenced by prose only — no asserted
# logic: triples here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

gmeow:Polarity
    a logic:AbstractIndividualType ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Polarity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    skos:definition "The assertoric-polarity axis of a standpoint claim — the direction in which the standpoint takes the proposition: gmeow:polarityAffirm (holds it), gmeow:polarityDeny (denies it), gmeow:polaritySuspend (withholds — neither affirms nor denies). One of the six orthogonal canonical claim-modality axes from which the legacy gmeow:StandpointModality projects. polarityDeny is frame-relative denial, NEVER a global-false verdict (Principle 9). Formalized by the Standpoint-Logic assertion sign in slices/grounding/logic — referenced here by prose only."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimPolarity gmeow:polarityDeny ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid reading gmeow:polarityDeny as a global truth verdict — it is one frame's denial, coexisting with rival affirmations (Principle 9) — and avoid conflating gmeow:polaritySuspend (an explicit withholding) with the absence of any claim."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Reference one seeded polarity individual from a gmeow:StandpointClaim via gmeow:claimPolarity, or from an annotated statement via gmeow:standpointPolarity; an absent value reads as gmeow:polarityAffirm."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the value vocabulary for the affirm / deny / suspend direction a standpoint takes toward a proposition — the axis from which the legacy gmeow:refuted (deny) is projected."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:polarityAffirm
    a gmeow:Polarity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "affirm"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint holds the proposition — takes it as the case. The affirmative polarity; the default when no gmeow:claimPolarity is given."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:polarityDeny
    a gmeow:Polarity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "deny"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint DENIES the proposition — frame-relative denial, distinct from silence (gmeow:polaritySuspend) and from low credence, NEVER a global-false verdict (Principle 9). The polarity from which the legacy gmeow:refuted projects."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:polaritySuspend
    a gmeow:Polarity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "suspend"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint neither affirms nor denies — withholds judgement. Distinct from gmeow:polarityDeny (an explicit denial) and from no claim at all. The polarity from which the legacy gmeow:conceivable projects."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:ModalForce
    a logic:AbstractIndividualType ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Modal Force"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    skos:definition "The alethic modal-force axis — the □/◊ register under which a standpoint holds a proposition: gmeow:modalForceNecessary (□, settled across every admitted precisification), gmeow:modalForceActual (holds in the actual case), gmeow:modalForcePossible (◊, holds in some admitted precisification), gmeow:modalForceCounterfactual (holds in a non-actual world). Orthogonal to gmeow:CredenceLevel (graded belief) and to gmeow:confidence (our certainty about the stance) — probability ≠ modal possibility ≠ confidence. One of the six axes; formalized by the Standpoint-Logic □_S/◊_S operators in slices/grounding/logic."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimModalForce gmeow:modalForcePossible ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid conflating gmeow:modalForcePossible (◊, an alethic register) with a low gmeow:CredenceLevel (graded belief) or with low gmeow:confidence (our certainty) — the three are orthogonal axes, not points on one scale."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Reference one seeded modal-force individual from a gmeow:StandpointClaim via gmeow:claimModalForce, or from an annotated statement via gmeow:standpointModalForce; an absent value reads as gmeow:modalForceNecessary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the value vocabulary for the alethic □/◊ register — necessary / actual / possible / counterfactual — under which a standpoint holds a proposition, kept distinct from credence and confidence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:modalForceNecessary
    a gmeow:ModalForce ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "necessary (□)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "□_S — the proposition is settled in every precisification the standpoint admits. The alethic force from which the legacy gmeow:unequivocal and gmeow:refuted project. The default when no gmeow:claimModalForce is given."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:modalForceActual
    a gmeow:ModalForce ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "actual"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The proposition holds in the actual case — neither raised to necessity nor weakened to mere possibility. The alethic force from which the legacy gmeow:probable and gmeow:bullshit project."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:modalForcePossible
    a gmeow:ModalForce ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "possible (◊)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "◊_S — the proposition holds in some precisification the standpoint admits, but is not settled. The alethic force from which the legacy gmeow:conceivable projects."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:modalForceCounterfactual
    a gmeow:ModalForce ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "counterfactual"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The proposition holds in a counterfactual / non-actual world — a supposition contrary to fact. Distinct from gmeow:modalForcePossible (◊ over admitted precisifications); no legacy gmeow:StandpointModality value projects from it, so a claim carrying it has no lossless legacy equivalent (hard-unsupported on projection)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:CredenceLevel
    a logic:AbstractIndividualType ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Credence Level"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    skos:definition "The qualitative credence-band axis — a closed companion vocabulary to the numeric gmeow:standpointCredence / gmeow:claimCredence (xsd:decimal in [0,1]): gmeow:credenceCertain, gmeow:credenceLikely, gmeow:credencePossible, gmeow:credenceUnspecified. The lossless legacy projection keys on the qualitative band (the AUTHORITATIVE projection surface); the decimal is the richer ADVISORY authoring surface. Canonical decimal-to-band thresholds: credenceUnspecified ⟺ no decimal present (credence axis left open); credencePossible ⟺ decimal in [0.0, 0.5); credenceLikely ⟺ decimal in [0.5, 0.9); credenceCertain ⟺ decimal in [0.9, 1.0]. Any decimal outside [0,1] is malformed. When BOTH a band and a decimal are present the decimal MUST fall within the band's range (enforced by gmeow:CredenceBandConsistencyShape). Authoring ONLY the decimal (no band) does NOT project to a legacy value — this is intentional non-approximation (Principle 9), not a silent default; author the band for projection. The thresholds make the band deterministically derivable from the decimal by any consumer that needs it. Distinct from gmeow:ModalForce (alethic register) and gmeow:confidence (our certainty about the stance). One of the six axes."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimCredenceLevel gmeow:credenceLikely ; gmeow:claimCredence 0.7 ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using a credence band as a global truth verdict, and avoid conflating it with gmeow:ModalForce (alethic □/◊) or gmeow:confidence (our certainty about the standpoint's stance) — graded belief, modal force, and confidence are three orthogonal axes. Avoid asserting a band and a decimal whose value falls outside the band's canonical threshold range."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Reference one band individual via gmeow:claimCredenceLevel (or gmeow:standpointCredenceLevel) for the projection-keying qualitative surface, and optionally carry the precise xsd:decimal via gmeow:claimCredence / gmeow:standpointCredence; when both are present the decimal must fall within the band's threshold range. The band is the AUTHORITATIVE projection key; the decimal is advisory finer-grained detail."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the closed qualitative band a standpoint's graded belief falls into — certain / likely / possible / unspecified — the AUTHORITATIVE surface the lossless legacy projection keys on, paired with the optional precise decimal that must lie within its threshold range."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:credenceCertain
    a gmeow:CredenceLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "certain"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint's graded belief is at or near the top of the credence scale — practically settled. Decimal credence in [0.9, 1.0]. The band from which the legacy gmeow:unequivocal and gmeow:refuted project."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:credenceLikely
    a gmeow:CredenceLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "likely"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint's graded belief is high but short of settled — decimal credence in [0.5, 0.9). The band from which the legacy gmeow:probable projects."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:credencePossible
    a gmeow:CredenceLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "possible"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint's graded belief is low — the proposition is entertained but not endorsed — decimal credence in [0.0, 0.5). The band from which the legacy gmeow:conceivable projects."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:credenceUnspecified
    a gmeow:CredenceLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "unspecified"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "No graded belief is asserted — the credence axis is left open; no decimal is present. Carrying a numeric decimal alongside this band is contradictory (a decimal asserts graded belief while this band asserts there is none) and is rejected by gmeow:CredenceBandConsistencyShape. The band from which the legacy gmeow:bullshit projects (the bullshitter has no credence stake in the proposition)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:AssertoricForce
    a logic:AbstractIndividualType ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Assertoric Force"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    skos:definition "The assertoric-force / speech-act axis — what the standpoint DOES with the proposition: gmeow:assertoricAssert (puts it forward as true), gmeow:assertoricConjecture (offers it tentatively), gmeow:assertoricAssume (supposes it for the sake of argument), gmeow:assertoricRetract (withdraws a prior assertion, retained not erased — Principle 10). One of the six axes."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimAssertoricForce gmeow:assertoricConjecture ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid conflating gmeow:assertoricAssume (a supposition not endorsed) with gmeow:assertoricAssert (an endorsement), and never delete a retracted assertion — gmeow:assertoricRetract closes it as a retained act (Principle 10)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Reference one seeded force individual from a gmeow:StandpointClaim via gmeow:claimAssertoricForce, or from an annotated statement via gmeow:standpointAssertoricForce; an absent value reads as gmeow:assertoricAssert."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the value vocabulary for the speech-act force — assert / conjecture / assume / retract — a standpoint applies to a proposition."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:assertoricAssert
    a gmeow:AssertoricForce ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "assert"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint puts the proposition forward as true — the default assertoric force from which the legacy gmeow:unequivocal, gmeow:refuted, and gmeow:bullshit project."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:assertoricConjecture
    a gmeow:AssertoricForce ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "conjecture"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint offers the proposition tentatively — a guess put up for testing. The force from which the legacy gmeow:probable projects."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:assertoricAssume
    a gmeow:AssertoricForce ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "assume"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint supposes the proposition for the sake of argument, without endorsing it. The force from which the legacy gmeow:conceivable projects."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:assertoricRetract
    a gmeow:AssertoricForce ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "retract"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint withdraws a prior assertion — retained as a closed act, never erased (Principle 10). No legacy gmeow:StandpointModality value projects from it, so a claim carrying it has no lossless legacy equivalent (hard-unsupported on projection)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:TruthDirectedness
    a logic:AbstractIndividualType ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Truth Directedness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    skos:definition "The truth-directedness axis — the standpoint's orientation toward the truth of the proposition: gmeow:truthAimed (aims at correspondence), gmeow:truthIndifferent (Frankfurt's bullshit — asserts with indifference to truth-value, neither true nor false under the stance), gmeow:truthStrategic (asserts to achieve an effect rather than to track truth). gmeow:truthIndifferent is what carries the legacy gmeow:bullshit — it is NOT a truth value and NOT a denial. One of the six axes."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness gmeow:truthIndifferent ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid treating gmeow:truthIndifferent as a polarity or a truth value — it is an orthogonal orientation (Frankfurt's bullshit); a bullshit claim still has gmeow:polarityAffirm. Avoid conflating gmeow:truthStrategic (instrumental care for truth) with gmeow:truthIndifferent (no care at all)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Reference one seeded orientation individual from a gmeow:StandpointClaim via gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness, or from an annotated statement via gmeow:standpointTruthDirectedness; an absent value reads as gmeow:truthAimed."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the value vocabulary for the standpoint's orientation toward truth — truth-aimed / indifferent / strategic — the axis that carries the legacy gmeow:bullshit (indifferent)."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:truthAimed
    a gmeow:TruthDirectedness ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "truth-aimed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint aims at correspondence — it asserts in order to track the truth. The orientation from which the four non-bullshit legacy values (gmeow:unequivocal, gmeow:probable, gmeow:conceivable, gmeow:refuted) project. The default when no gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness is given."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:truthIndifferent
    a gmeow:TruthDirectedness ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "indifferent (bullshit)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Frankfurt's bullshit — the standpoint asserts with indifference to the truth-value of the proposition, neither true nor false under the stance. This axis value — NOT a polarity, NOT a truth value — is what carries the legacy gmeow:bullshit; a bullshit claim still affirms (gmeow:polarityAffirm) with an open credence (gmeow:credenceUnspecified)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:truthStrategic
    a gmeow:TruthDirectedness ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "strategic"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint asserts to achieve an effect (persuasion, manoeuvre) rather than to track truth, while still caring instrumentally about it. Distinct from gmeow:truthIndifferent (no care at all); no legacy gmeow:StandpointModality value projects from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:SupportStatus
    a logic:AbstractIndividualType ,
        owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "Support Status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    skos:definition "The Belnap evidential-support axis — the four-valued status of proof / counterproof a standpoint has for the proposition: gmeow:supportSupported (proof, no counterproof), gmeow:supportOpposed (counterproof, no proof), gmeow:supportBoth (a witnessed glut — proof AND counterproof coexist within one frame), gmeow:supportNeither (a gap — neither). gmeow:supportBoth is admissible. Self-contained gmeow domain vocabulary aligned by prose reference to logic:InformationState; one of the six axes."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimSupportStatus gmeow:supportBoth ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid reading gmeow:supportOpposed as a global-false verdict (it is one frame's counterproof, Principle 9), and avoid suppressing gmeow:supportBoth — a witnessed contradiction within a frame is admissible, not an error to be normalised away."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Reference one seeded status individual from a gmeow:StandpointClaim via gmeow:claimSupportStatus, or from an annotated statement via gmeow:standpointSupportStatus; the Belnap glut gmeow:supportBoth and gap gmeow:supportNeither are both legal values."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the value vocabulary for the Belnap evidential status — supported / opposed / both / neither — a standpoint has for a proposition, aligned by prose to logic:InformationState."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:supportSupported
    a gmeow:SupportStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "supported"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Belnap: a proof and no counterproof. The evidential state from which the legacy gmeow:unequivocal and gmeow:probable project."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Corresponds (by prose reference, Principle 5) to the now-live logic:InfoSupported — the Belnap reasoning-result information state this domain support status mirrors; the typed bridge stays a logic:formalizes back-reference from the logic slice, never an asserted logic: triple here."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:supportOpposed
    a gmeow:SupportStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "opposed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Belnap: a counterproof and no proof. The evidential state from which the legacy gmeow:refuted projects — frame-relative, never a global-false verdict (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Corresponds (by prose reference, Principle 5) to the now-live logic:InfoOpposed — the Belnap reasoning-result information state this domain support status mirrors; the typed bridge stays a logic:formalizes back-reference from the logic slice, never an asserted logic: triple here."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:supportBoth
    a gmeow:SupportStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "both"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Belnap: a witnessed glut — proof AND counterproof coexist within one frame. Admissible; no legacy gmeow:StandpointModality value projects from it, so a claim carrying it has no lossless legacy equivalent (hard-unsupported on projection)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Corresponds (by prose reference, Principle 5) to the now-live logic:InfoBoth — the Belnap reasoning-result information state this domain support status mirrors; the typed bridge stays a logic:formalizes back-reference from the logic slice, never an asserted logic: triple here."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

gmeow:supportNeither
    a gmeow:SupportStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "neither"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Belnap: a gap — neither proof nor counterproof. The evidential state from which the legacy gmeow:conceivable and gmeow:bullshit project."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Corresponds (by prose reference, Principle 5) to the now-live logic:InfoNeither — the Belnap reasoning-result information state this domain support status mirrors; the typed bridge stays a logic:formalizes back-reference from the logic slice, never an asserted logic: triple here."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ,
        gmeow:boxCBox .

# ── Annotation twins (flattened / annotated-statement form, mirror gmeow:standpointModality) ──

gmeow:standpointPolarity
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "standpoint polarity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Polarity ;
    skos:definition "The affirm / deny / suspend direction a standpoint takes toward the annotated proposition. The flattened-statement twin of gmeow:claimPolarity; absent reads as gmeow:polarityAffirm. polarityDeny is frame-relative denial, never global-false (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ,
        gmeow:concernStatementMetadata ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:standpointModalForce
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "standpoint modal force"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:ModalForce ;
    skos:definition "The alethic □/◊ register under which a standpoint holds the annotated proposition. The flattened-statement twin of gmeow:claimModalForce; absent reads as gmeow:modalForceNecessary. Orthogonal to credence and gmeow:confidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ,
        gmeow:concernStatementMetadata ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:standpointCredence
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "standpoint credence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    skos:definition "The precise graded belief (xsd:decimal in [0,1]) a standpoint assigns the annotated proposition — the ADVISORY authoring surface paired with the AUTHORITATIVE qualitative gmeow:standpointCredenceLevel band the lossless projection keys on. When both are present the decimal MUST fall within the band's canonical threshold range: credencePossible [0.0, 0.5), credenceLikely [0.5, 0.9), credenceCertain [0.9, 1.0]. Authoring only the decimal (no band) does NOT project to a legacy value — intentional non-approximation (Principle 9). Decimals outside [0,1] are malformed. Distinct from gmeow:ModalForce (alethic register) and gmeow:confidence (our certainty about the stance)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ,
        gmeow:concernStatementMetadata ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:standpointCredenceLevel
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "standpoint credence level"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:CredenceLevel ;
    skos:definition "The qualitative credence band a standpoint assigns the annotated proposition — the projection-keying twin of gmeow:standpointCredence. The flattened-statement twin of gmeow:claimCredenceLevel."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ,
        gmeow:concernStatementMetadata ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:standpointAssertoricForce
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "standpoint assertoric force"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:AssertoricForce ;
    skos:definition "The speech-act force — assert / conjecture / assume / retract — a standpoint applies to the annotated proposition. The flattened-statement twin of gmeow:claimAssertoricForce; absent reads as gmeow:assertoricAssert."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ,
        gmeow:concernStatementMetadata ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:standpointTruthDirectedness
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "standpoint truth directedness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:TruthDirectedness ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint's orientation toward the truth of the annotated proposition — truth-aimed / indifferent / strategic. The flattened-statement twin of gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness; absent reads as gmeow:truthAimed. gmeow:truthIndifferent carries the legacy gmeow:bullshit."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ,
        gmeow:concernStatementMetadata ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:standpointSupportStatus
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "standpoint support status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:SupportStatus ;
    skos:definition "The Belnap evidential status — supported / opposed / both / neither — a standpoint has for the annotated proposition. The flattened-statement twin of gmeow:claimSupportStatus. Aligned by prose to logic:InformationState."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ,
        gmeow:concernStatementMetadata ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox .

# ── Reified twins (StandpointClaim form, mirror gmeow:claimModality; functional; NOT subPropertyOf observationResult) ──

gmeow:claimPolarity
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "claim polarity"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:Polarity ;
    skos:definition "The affirm / deny / suspend polarity assigned to a gmeow:StandpointClaim. Not declared rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:observationResult because gmeow:Polarity (a logic:QualityValue / abstract individual) is disjoint from gmeow:Entity in the DL profile. When the claim is flattened, claimPolarity becomes gmeow:standpointPolarity. gmeow:polarityDeny is the canonical carrier of the legacy gmeow:refuted — frame-relative, never global-false (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:lieHeldClaim gmeow:claimPolarity gmeow:polarityDeny ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid asserting two polarities — it is functional — and avoid reading gmeow:polarityDeny as a global truth verdict; it denies the claim from this frame only (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point the StandpointClaim at one gmeow:Polarity individual; absent reads as gmeow:polarityAffirm, and on flattening it becomes gmeow:standpointPolarity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to assign the affirm / deny / suspend direction a gmeow:StandpointClaim takes — the reified-relator counterpart of gmeow:standpointPolarity and the canonical carrier of the legacy refuted (deny)."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:claimModalForce
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "claim modal force"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:ModalForce ;
    skos:definition "The alethic □/◊ modal force assigned to a gmeow:StandpointClaim. Not rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:observationResult (DL disjointness, as gmeow:claimModality). When the claim is flattened, it becomes gmeow:standpointModalForce. Orthogonal to credence and gmeow:confidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimModalForce gmeow:modalForceNecessary ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid asserting two modal forces — it is functional — and avoid conflating gmeow:modalForcePossible with a low credence band or low gmeow:confidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point the StandpointClaim at one gmeow:ModalForce individual; absent reads as gmeow:modalForceNecessary, and on flattening it becomes gmeow:standpointModalForce."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to assign the alethic □/◊ register a gmeow:StandpointClaim carries — the reified-relator counterpart of gmeow:standpointModalForce, kept distinct from credence and confidence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:claimCredence
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "claim credence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    skos:definition "The precise graded belief (xsd:decimal in [0,1]) assigned to a gmeow:StandpointClaim — the ADVISORY authoring surface paired with the AUTHORITATIVE qualitative gmeow:claimCredenceLevel band the projection keys on. When both are present the decimal MUST fall within the band's canonical threshold range: credencePossible [0.0, 0.5), credenceLikely [0.5, 0.9), credenceCertain [0.9, 1.0]. Authoring only the decimal (no band) does NOT project to a legacy value — intentional non-approximation (Principle 9); author the band for projection. Decimals outside [0,1] are malformed and rejected by gmeow:ClaimCredenceRangeShape. When the claim is flattened, it becomes gmeow:standpointCredence. Distinct from gmeow:ModalForce and gmeow:confidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimCredence 0.7 ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid asserting two credence values — it is functional — and avoid treating the decimal as a global truth verdict; pair it with gmeow:claimCredenceLevel, which the lossless legacy projection actually keys on. Avoid decimals outside [0,1] (malformed) and avoid pairing a decimal with a band whose threshold range it does not satisfy."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Carry the precise decimal in [0,1] on the StandpointClaim alongside the qualitative gmeow:claimCredenceLevel band; the decimal must lie within the band's threshold range (credencePossible [0,0.5), credenceLikely [0.5,0.9), credenceCertain [0.9,1.0]). On flattening it becomes gmeow:standpointCredence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to record the precise numeric credence a gmeow:StandpointClaim carries — the advisory finer-grained surface that must be consistent with the authoritative qualitative band whose threshold range contains it."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:claimCredenceLevel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "claim credence level"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:CredenceLevel ;
    skos:definition "The qualitative credence band assigned to a gmeow:StandpointClaim — the projection-keying twin of gmeow:claimCredence. Not rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:observationResult (DL disjointness). When the claim is flattened, it becomes gmeow:standpointCredenceLevel."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimCredenceLevel gmeow:credenceLikely ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid asserting two bands — it is functional — and avoid using the band as a global truth verdict; it is one frame's graded belief."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point the StandpointClaim at one gmeow:CredenceLevel band, optionally alongside the precise gmeow:claimCredence; on flattening it becomes gmeow:standpointCredenceLevel."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to assign the qualitative credence band a gmeow:StandpointClaim carries — the surface the lossless legacy projection keys on."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:claimAssertoricForce
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "claim assertoric force"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:AssertoricForce ;
    skos:definition "The speech-act force — assert / conjecture / assume / retract — assigned to a gmeow:StandpointClaim. Not rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:observationResult (DL disjointness). When the claim is flattened, it becomes gmeow:standpointAssertoricForce."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimAssertoricForce gmeow:assertoricConjecture ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid asserting two forces — it is functional — and never delete a retracted assertion; gmeow:assertoricRetract closes it as a retained act (Principle 10)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point the StandpointClaim at one gmeow:AssertoricForce individual; absent reads as gmeow:assertoricAssert, and on flattening it becomes gmeow:standpointAssertoricForce."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to assign the speech-act force a gmeow:StandpointClaim carries — the reified-relator counterpart of gmeow:standpointAssertoricForce."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "claim truth directedness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:TruthDirectedness ;
    skos:definition "The standpoint's orientation toward truth — truth-aimed / indifferent / strategic — assigned to a gmeow:StandpointClaim. Not rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:observationResult (DL disjointness). When the claim is flattened, it becomes gmeow:standpointTruthDirectedness. gmeow:truthIndifferent is the canonical carrier of the legacy gmeow:bullshit."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:bullshitClaim gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness gmeow:truthIndifferent ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid asserting two orientations — it is functional — and avoid treating gmeow:truthIndifferent as a polarity or truth value; a bullshit claim still affirms (gmeow:polarityAffirm)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point the StandpointClaim at one gmeow:TruthDirectedness individual; absent reads as gmeow:truthAimed, and on flattening it becomes gmeow:standpointTruthDirectedness."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to assign the standpoint's truth-orientation a gmeow:StandpointClaim carries — the canonical carrier of the legacy bullshit (indifferent)."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:claimSupportStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "claim support status"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:SupportStatus ;
    skos:definition "The Belnap evidential status — supported / opposed / both / neither — assigned to a gmeow:StandpointClaim. Not rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:observationResult (DL disjointness). When the claim is flattened, it becomes gmeow:standpointSupportStatus. Aligned by prose to logic:InformationState."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:claim gmeow:claimSupportStatus gmeow:supportBoth ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid asserting two statuses — it is functional — and avoid normalising away gmeow:supportBoth; a witnessed glut within a frame is admissible (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Point the StandpointClaim at one gmeow:SupportStatus individual; the glut gmeow:supportBoth and gap gmeow:supportNeither are both legal, and on flattening it becomes gmeow:standpointSupportStatus."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to assign the Belnap evidential status a gmeow:StandpointClaim carries — the reified-relator counterpart of gmeow:standpointSupportStatus, aligned by prose to logic:InformationState."@x-gmeow-english .

# ── Decomposition bundle property: each legacy gmeow:StandpointModality value declares its canonical six-axis decomposition (mirror of logic:expandsToFacet). The lossless projection in crates/slice/src/standpoint_modality.rs cross-checks the Rust table against these bundles. ──

gmeow:decomposesToAxis
    a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "decomposes to axis"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a legacy gmeow:StandpointModality value to its canonical six-axis decomposition — one value individual from each of gmeow:Polarity, gmeow:ModalForce, gmeow:CredenceLevel, gmeow:AssertoricForce, gmeow:TruthDirectedness, gmeow:SupportStatus. The declarative source of truth (mirror of logic:expandsToFacet) the Rust lossless projection round-trips against. The range is intentionally open (the six axis value-classes); an annotation property to keep the OWL downcast DL-clean."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:docsConcern gmeow:concernStandpoints ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:heldIn
    a fno:Function ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "held in"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A boolean SPARQL extension function, gmeow:heldIn(reifier, standpoint): true iff the reified statement's gmeow:accordingTo vantage is the given standpoint, or a standpoint that gmeow:sharpens it — so a claim held in a sharper frame counts as held in the broader one. A direct, non-transitive membership test over the already-reasoned graph: the gmeow:sharpens closure is materialised upstream by the reasoner, never recomputed by the query, so the native logic solver stays the sole reasoning authority."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "FILTER( gmeow:heldIn(?r, gmeow:universalStandpoint) )"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using it as a reasoning primitive — it does NOT compute the gmeow:sharpens transitive closure; if the closure is not materialised in the queried graph it will under-report, so reason first, then query."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Bind a reifier with `?r rdf:reifies <<( ?s ?p ?o )>>`, then call gmeow:heldIn(?r, <standpoint>) in a FILTER; combine with GRAPH <world> to scope a single world while testing standpoint membership."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to scope a SPARQL query to the claims held in a standpoint (or any sharper standpoint) — the query-surface counterpart of the gmeow:accordingTo / gmeow:sharpens standpoint poset."@x-gmeow-english .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> ;
    rdfs:comment """Cross-cutting foundational facility (a peer of the temporal module): the standpoint axis — *according to whom* a statement is held true. It lands in the statement/provenance layer and is consumed by every slice that records contested facts (events, locations, genealogy, organizations, trust, naming).

DOCTRINE.
  * Three orthogonal axes, no inferential bridge: gmeow:accordingTo (whose frame) ⟂ gmeow:wasAttributedTo (which source recorded it) ⟂ gmeow:confidence (how sure we are).
  * Two clocks kept apart: fact-time (gmeow:validFrom / gmeow:validUntil — when the claimed fact holds) ⟂ standpoint-time (when the standpoint held the position — light via validFrom/Until on the statement, heavy via a reified gmeow:StandpointTenure).
  * No single slot to win (CONSTITUTION Principle 9): a contested fact is several standpoint-indexed claims that coexist; there is no preferredRank / primary* selector.
  * Suppression, never erasure (Principle 10): a withdrawn claim or a closed tenure sets gmeow:displayable false; it is retained, not deleted.
  * DL-clean by construction (Principle 3): the standpoint axis is an owl:AnnotationProperty, so the generated OWL downcast stays OWL 2 DL.
  * Factored modality: claim modality is six orthogonal canonical axes — gmeow:Polarity (affirm/deny/suspend) ⟂ gmeow:ModalForce (necessary/actual/possible/counterfactual) ⟂ gmeow:CredenceLevel + numeric gmeow:standpointCredence ⟂ gmeow:AssertoricForce (assert/conjecture/assume/retract) ⟂ gmeow:TruthDirectedness (truth-aimed/indifferent/strategic) ⟂ gmeow:SupportStatus (Belnap supported/opposed/both/neither). The legacy five-value gmeow:StandpointModality is RETAINED as a lossless projection of the axes (each value carries its canonical decomposition via gmeow:decomposesToAxis; the projection is round-tripped in crates/slice/src/standpoint_modality.rs, which hard-fails any axis tuple with no legacy equivalent rather than approximating). bullshit = truthDirectedness indifferent (not a truth value); refuted = polarity deny (frame-relative, never global-false). The logic: machinery (Standpoint-Logic □/◊, Belnap support) stays central in slices/grounding/logic, referenced here by prose only — no asserted logic: triples.

FORMAL GROUNDING. The facility realises Standpoint Logic (Gómez Álvarez & Rudolph): gmeow:accordingTo is the axiom-level standpoint label (cf. Standpoint-OWL 2 standpointLabel); gmeow:standpointModality unequivocal / conceivable are the □_S / ◊_S operators (gmeow:modalForceNecessary / gmeow:modalForcePossible on the factored axis); gmeow:sharpens is the standpoint ⊆ / precisification relation; gmeow:universalStandpoint is the universal standpoint *. See docs/standpoints.md."""@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Standpoint Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The GMEOW Standpoint Module — classes, properties, and individuals of the GMEOW super-vocabulary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ,
        gmeow:boxConfigBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox .

# Closed-world cardinality/value axioms backing the hand-authored SHACL
# well-formedness shapes.
gmeow:StandpointTenure rdfs:subClassOf
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty gmeow:tenureStandpoint ; owl:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; owl:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty gmeow:standpointClaim ; owl:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; owl:onClass gmeow:StandpointClaim ] .

# exact-one minCount restoration: min-qualified sibling restrictions
# restoring sh:minCount for the reasoner-safe max-qualified exact-one antecedents.
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/StandpointTenure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> [ <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> ; <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/tenureStandpoint> ; <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#minQualifiedCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ; <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> ] .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/StandpointTenure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> [ <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> ; <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/standpointClaim> ; <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#minQualifiedCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ; <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/StandpointClaim> ] .

# =========================================================================== #
# Procedural constraints authored as raw logic:Formula integrity trees. Each   #
# carries logic:formalizes so its projected sh:SPARQLConstraint twin keys onto  #
# the same source-term as the hand-authored SHACL it replaces. The [0,1] range  #
# is split into a lower- and an upper-bound constraint so each lowers to a      #
# single bound-value FILTER (a disjunction of pure filters would produce UNION  #
# arms that re-bind nothing).                                                   #
# =========================================================================== #

# gmeow:claimCredence must be an xsd:decimal >= 0.0 (lower bound of the unit
# interval); a value below 0 is malformed.
gmeow:ClaimCredenceLowerBoundConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Claim credence lower-bound constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: gmeow:claimCredence must be an xsd:decimal at or above 0.0."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:ClaimCredenceRangeShape ;
    logic:message "gmeow:claimCredence must be an xsd:decimal in [0.0, 1.0] — a credence value outside this range is malformed." ;
    logic:integrity logic:cclForall .
logic:cclForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:cclImpl .
logic:cclImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:cclGuard ; logic:consequent logic:cclLow .
logic:cclGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:claimCredence ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] .
logic:cclLow a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termGreaterEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "0.0" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:decimal ] .

# gmeow:claimCredence must be an xsd:decimal <= 1.0 (upper bound of the unit
# interval); a value above 1 is malformed.
gmeow:ClaimCredenceUpperBoundConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Claim credence upper-bound constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: gmeow:claimCredence must be an xsd:decimal at or below 1.0."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:ClaimCredenceRangeShape ;
    logic:message "gmeow:claimCredence must be an xsd:decimal in [0.0, 1.0] — a credence value outside this range is malformed." ;
    logic:integrity logic:ccuForall .
logic:ccuForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:ccuImpl .
logic:ccuImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:ccuGuard ; logic:consequent logic:ccuHigh .
logic:ccuGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:claimCredence ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] .
logic:ccuHigh a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termLessEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "1.0" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:decimal ] .

# gmeow:standpointCredence must be an xsd:decimal >= 0.0.
gmeow:StandpointCredenceLowerBoundConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Standpoint credence lower-bound constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: gmeow:standpointCredence must be an xsd:decimal at or above 0.0."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:StandpointCredenceRangeShape ;
    logic:message "gmeow:standpointCredence must be an xsd:decimal in [0.0, 1.0] — a credence value outside this range is malformed." ;
    logic:integrity logic:sclForall .
logic:sclForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:sclImpl .
logic:sclImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:sclGuard ; logic:consequent logic:sclLow .
logic:sclGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:standpointCredence ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] .
logic:sclLow a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termGreaterEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "0.0" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:decimal ] .

# gmeow:standpointCredence must be an xsd:decimal <= 1.0.
gmeow:StandpointCredenceUpperBoundConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Standpoint credence upper-bound constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: gmeow:standpointCredence must be an xsd:decimal at or below 1.0."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:StandpointCredenceRangeShape ;
    logic:message "gmeow:standpointCredence must be an xsd:decimal in [0.0, 1.0] — a credence value outside this range is malformed." ;
    logic:integrity logic:scuForall .
logic:scuForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:scuImpl .
logic:scuImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:scuGuard ; logic:consequent logic:scuHigh .
logic:scuGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:standpointCredence ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] .
logic:scuHigh a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termLessEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "v" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "1.0" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:decimal ] .

# A withdrawn standpoint (a gmeow:StandpointTenure whose interval has ended)
# should set gmeow:displayable false — suppressed from display, never deleted. Warning.
gmeow:WithdrawnStandpointSuppressionConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Withdrawn standpoint suppression constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: a gmeow:StandpointTenure whose interval has ended sets gmeow:displayable false."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:WithdrawnStandpointSuppressionShape ;
    logic:severity "Warning" ;
    logic:message "A withdrawn standpoint (a StandpointTenure whose interval has ended) should set gmeow:displayable false — suppressed from display, never deleted." ;
    logic:integrity logic:wssForall .
logic:wssForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "iv" ] , [ logic:termIndex 2 ; logic:termVariable "end" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:wssImpl .
logic:wssImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:wssGuard ; logic:consequent logic:wssDisp .
logic:wssGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:wssType , logic:wssDuring , logic:wssEnded .
logic:wssType a logic:Formula ; logic:relation <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:StandpointTenure ] .
logic:wssDuring a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:duringInterval ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "iv" ] .
logic:wssEnded a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:endedAtTime ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "iv" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "end" ] .
logic:wssDisp a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:displayable ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "false" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> ] .

# =========================================================================== #
# Procedural constraint authored as a raw logic:Formula integrity tree, #
# projected to a sh:SPARQLConstraint keyed (via logic:formalizes) onto the same  #
# gmeow:CredenceBandConsistencyShape source-term the hand-authored SHACL         #
# enforced. When a claim carries BOTH a qualitative band and a numeric decimal,  #
# the decimal must fall within the band's canonical threshold range. The band    #
# check is a pure filter disjunction, lowered to one combined FILTER.            #
# =========================================================================== #

gmeow:ClaimCredenceBandConsistencyConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "Claim credence band consistency constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: when a claim asserts both a qualitative gmeow:claimCredenceLevel band and a numeric gmeow:claimCredence decimal, the decimal must fall within the band's canonical threshold range (credencePossible [0,0.5), credenceLikely [0.5,0.9), credenceCertain [0.9,1.0]); credenceUnspecified must carry no decimal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:CredenceBandConsistencyShape ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "Credence band and decimal are inconsistent: the decimal must fall within the band's canonical range (credencePossible [0,0.5), credenceLikely [0.5,0.9), credenceCertain [0.9,1.0]) and credenceUnspecified must carry no decimal at all." ;
    logic:integrity logic:ccbForall .
logic:ccbForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:ccbImpl .
logic:ccbImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:ccbGuard ; logic:consequent logic:ccbPhi .
logic:ccbGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:claimCredenceLevel ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "bg" ] .
logic:ccbPhi a logic:Formula ; logic:not logic:ccbEx .
logic:ccbEx a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "band" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "dec" ] ;
    logic:exists logic:ccbBody .
logic:ccbBody a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:ccbLevel , logic:ccbDec , logic:ccbBad .
logic:ccbLevel a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:claimCredenceLevel ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "band" ] .
logic:ccbDec a logic:Formula ; logic:relation gmeow:claimCredence ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "dec" ] .
logic:ccbBad a logic:Formula ; logic:or logic:ccbCertain , logic:ccbLikely , logic:ccbPossible , logic:ccbUnspec .
# credenceCertain [0.9, 1.0] — a decimal below 0.9 is inconsistent.
logic:ccbCertain a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:ccbIsCertain , logic:ccbCertainLo .
logic:ccbIsCertain a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "band" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:credenceCertain ] .
logic:ccbCertainLo a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termLess ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "dec" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "0.9" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:decimal ] .
# credenceLikely [0.5, 0.9) — a decimal below 0.5 or at/above 0.9 is inconsistent.
logic:ccbLikely a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:ccbIsLikely , logic:ccbLikelyRange .
logic:ccbIsLikely a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "band" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:credenceLikely ] .
logic:ccbLikelyRange a logic:Formula ; logic:or logic:ccbLikelyLo , logic:ccbLikelyHi .
logic:ccbLikelyLo a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termLess ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "dec" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "0.5" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:decimal ] .
logic:ccbLikelyHi a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termGreaterEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "dec" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "0.9" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:decimal ] .
# credencePossible [0.0, 0.5) — a decimal below 0.0 or at/above 0.5 is inconsistent.
logic:ccbPossible a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:ccbIsPossible , logic:ccbPossibleRange .
logic:ccbIsPossible a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "band" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:credencePossible ] .
logic:ccbPossibleRange a logic:Formula ; logic:or logic:ccbPossibleLo , logic:ccbPossibleHi .
logic:ccbPossibleLo a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termLess ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "dec" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "0.0" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:decimal ] .
logic:ccbPossibleHi a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termGreaterEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "dec" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "0.5" ; logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:decimal ] .
# credenceUnspecified — any decimal at all is inconsistent (no graded belief present).
logic:ccbUnspec a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termEqual ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "band" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termIri gmeow:credenceUnspecified ] .

# =========================================================================== #
# Procedural constraint: no claim may be marked preferred/primary —      #
# standpoint-indexed claims are co-equal, there is no single slot to win          #
# (Principle 9). Any predicate under the gmeow:primary* or gmeow:preferred*        #
# namespace is forbidden. Projected onto the gmeow:NoPreferredClaimShape          #
# source-term. The focus has no class form, so it is selected by a raw            #
# logic:sparqlTarget; the body forbids the variable-predicate witness via         #
# logic:linkVia + a logic:termStrStarts prefix disjunction.                       #
# =========================================================================== #

gmeow:NoPreferredClaimConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:label "No preferred / primary claim constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    skos:definition "A closed-world integrity constraint: no node may carry a predicate under the gmeow:primary or gmeow:preferred namespace — standpoint-indexed claims are co-equal (Principle 9)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:NoPreferredClaimShape ;
    logic:severity "Violation" ;
    logic:message "No claim may be marked preferred/primary; standpoint-indexed claims are co-equal — there is no single slot to win (Principle 9)." ;
    logic:integrity logic:npcForall .
logic:npcForall a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] ;
    logic:forall logic:npcImpl .
logic:npcImpl a logic:Formula ; logic:antecedent logic:npcGuard ; logic:consequent logic:npcPhi .
logic:npcGuard a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:sparqlTarget ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "SELECT ?this WHERE { ?this ?p ?o . FILTER ( STRSTARTS(STR(?p), 'https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/primary') || STRSTARTS(STR(?p), 'https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/preferred') ) }" ] .
logic:npcPhi a logic:Formula ; logic:not logic:npcEx .
logic:npcEx a logic:Formula ;
    logic:quantifiedVariable [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "p" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "o" ] ;
    logic:exists logic:npcBody .
logic:npcBody a logic:Formula ; logic:and logic:npcLink , logic:npcPrefix .
logic:npcLink a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:linkVia ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "this" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termVariable "p" ] , [ logic:termIndex 2 ; logic:termVariable "o" ] .
logic:npcPrefix a logic:Formula ; logic:or logic:npcPrimary , logic:npcPreferred .
logic:npcPrimary a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termStrStarts ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "p" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/primary" ] .
logic:npcPreferred a logic:Formula ; logic:relation logic:termStrStarts ;
    logic:argument [ logic:termIndex 0 ; logic:termVariable "p" ] , [ logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termLiteral "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/preferred" ] .

# --- Shape-migration grounding (projected to generated/shapes/validation-shapes.ttl) ---
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/StandpointTenure> logic:subClassOf [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/standpointClaim> ; logic:allValuesFrom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/StandpointClaim> ] .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/StandpointTenure> logic:subClassOf [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/tenureStandpoint> ; logic:allValuesFrom <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> ] .
[ a <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureEntry> ; <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onClass> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/StandpointTenure> ; <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureKey> "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/standpointClaim" ; <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureValue> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosedWorldClosure> ] .
[ a <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureEntry> ; <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onClass> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/StandpointTenure> ; <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureKey> "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/tenureStandpoint" ; <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureValue> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosedWorldClosure> ] .


# --- Wave B1 shape-drain: standpoint-tenure cardinality restoration ---
# gmeow:StandpointTenureShape — a StandpointTenure records exactly one standpoint and exactly one
# generated StandpointClaim.
gmeow:StandpointTenure logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:tenureStandpoint ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:standpointClaim ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass owl:Thing ] .

# ── logic: assertion carriers for this slice's own terms ────────────────────────
# The canonical logic: carriers for the characteristics and integrity conditions of the
# terms THIS slice owns. Each record names one of this slice's own properties or classes
# through a logic: RBox predicate; the native coherence gate joins the record to enforce
# the condition, and the OWL grounding view projects owl:FunctionalProperty (and friends)
# from it. Authored here rather than in the logic slice because the fact asserted is a
# fact about this slice's own term, and a grounding slice never depends on a non-grounding
# slice (docs/GROUNDING.md, the tier rule): the logic: assertion vocabulary is CONSUMED
# here (gmeow:sliceDependsOn logic), never owned.
#   logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion — logic:characterizes names the property, logic:characteristicSort its characteristic.

gmeow:sharpensTransitivity
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "sharpens is transitive"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:sharpens is transitive: the standpoint refinement order its skos:definition names (Standpoint Logic's coverage relation). The native coherence gate reads this to close the refinement order. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:sharpens ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:transitiveProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:sharpens ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:sharpens composes along chains; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when the relation must not compose — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:sharpens, logic:characteristicSort logic:transitiveProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:sharpens and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:sharpens (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:sharpensTransitivity logic:characterizes gmeow:sharpens ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:claimAssertoricForceFunctionality
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/standpoint> ;
    rdfs:label "claimAssertoricForce is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:claimAssertoricForce is functional: a standpoint claim carries one speech-act force — assert, conjecture, assume, or retract — so the relator takes a single force (absent reading as assert) and a retracted assertion is closed as a retained act rather than gaining a rival force."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:claimAssertoricForce ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:claimAssertoricForce ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:claimAssertoricForce names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:claimAssertoricForce, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:claimAssertoricForce and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:claimAssertoricForce (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:claimAssertoricForceFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:claimAssertoricForce ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:claimCredenceFunctionality
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
